Subject: add a route forwarding four allowlisted collective_rpc methods

Applies to: prime-rl 26b3131d2716a4f8210b165df584b83b4bc54f61 (tag v0.9.1.dev41)
Apply with: patch -p1 < 02-collective-rpc-route.patch
Touches: src/prime_rl/inference/vllm/server.py, one hunk, adds
         FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS, `_encode_rpc_result`, and the
         `/collective_rpc` route

WHAT AND WHY
prime-rl exposes collective_rpc over HTTP at three routes (/update_weights,
/liveness, /init_broadcaster) and each hardcodes one method name, so none of
them can reach a method added by a worker extension. Extraction needs to call
`install_logits_hook` and `retrieve_and_clear_logits` on the workers; without a
forwarding route there is no path to either.

Bytes are the reason for the encoder: `retrieve_and_clear_logits` returns a
(dtype, shape, raw bytes) triple, and JSON cannot carry the third element. It is
base64-encoded under a `__bytes_b64__` key so the client can distinguish an
encoded blob from an ordinary list.

WHAT IS FORWARDED
Exactly the four methods in FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS: install_logits_hook,
retrieve_and_clear_logits, uninstall_logits_hook, get_scheduler_config_summary.
Anything else is refused with HTTP 400 naming what is allowed. The route is a
seam for logit extraction, not general worker access, and the allowlist is what
makes that true in the code rather than only in this header. It is also
continuous with the file it lands in: the three routes above each name one
method, and this one names four.

`JSONResponse` is already imported by this module, so the refusal adds no import.
--- a/src/prime_rl/inference/vllm/server.py
+++ b/src/prime_rl/inference/vllm/server.py
@@ -147,6 +147,61 @@
     return {"status": "ok"}
 
 
+# The only worker methods /collective_rpc will forward. The three routes above
+# each name exactly one method; this names four rather than accepting any, so
+# the route stays a seam for logit extraction instead of general worker access.
+FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS = frozenset(
+    {
+        "install_logits_hook",
+        "retrieve_and_clear_logits",
+        "uninstall_logits_hook",
+        "get_scheduler_config_summary",
+    }
+)
+
+
+def _encode_rpc_result(value):
+    """JSON-safe form of one rank's collective_rpc return value.
+
+    Raw bytes are the reason this exists: a worker extension that returns tensor
+    data returns it as bytes, and JSON cannot carry those. Encoded as base64
+    with a tagged wrapper so the client can tell an encoded blob from a list.
+    """
+    import base64
+
+    if isinstance(value, bytes):
+        return {"__bytes_b64__": base64.b64encode(value).decode("ascii")}
+    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):
+        return [_encode_rpc_result(item) for item in value]
+    if isinstance(value, dict):
+        return {key: _encode_rpc_result(item) for key, item in value.items()}
+    return value
+
+
+@router.post("/collective_rpc")
+async def collective_rpc(request: Request):
+    """Forward one allowlisted collective_rpc call to the workers.
+
+    The three routes above each hardcode a single method name, so none of them
+    reaches a method added by a worker extension. This forwards any of the four
+    in FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS and refuses everything else.
+    """
+    data = await request.json()
+    method = data["method"]
+    if method not in FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS:
+        return JSONResponse(
+            {
+                "error": f"method {method!r} is not forwardable",
+                "allowed": sorted(FORWARDABLE_RPC_METHODS),
+            },
+            status_code=400,
+        )
+    args = tuple(data.get("args", []))
+    timeout = data.get("timeout")
+    results = await engine_client(request).collective_rpc(method, timeout=timeout, args=args)
+    return {"results": [_encode_rpc_result(result) for result in results]}
+
+
 async def custom_init_app_state(
     engine_client: EngineClient,
     state: State,
